gBw(){return new A.cm(["Part of this route repeats again and again. Find the pattern and use a loop to write a short, exact program.","Find the repeating pattern","Watch which moves BIT repeats every few steps and put them in a for loop. There may be a few steps to take before the loop.","Pattern Stairs"])},
gBB(){return new A.cm(["The first half and the second half of the route each repeat their own moves. Split them and use one loop for each.","Two loops","First find where the moves change and cut the route in two. For each part, find the repeated moves and how many times they repeat.","Two Patterns"])},
gBt(){return new A.cm(["An energy cell waits at the end of each side path. BIT must walk in, back out, then go on to the next side path.","There and back in a loop","Look at the first side path only: how many steps in, how many back, and how many forward to the next one? Put that whole part in a for loop, then count the side paths.","Side Path Errands"])},
By(a){var s=a.b
return new A.cm(["The river twists and turns with no fixed pattern. Write a rule so BIT picks its own direction at every step.","if checks","Inside the loop, use if hero.canMove('"+s+"'): to check whether BIT can move "+s+". If it can, go; if not, take the other direction. It's fine to loop a few extra times.","Misty River"])},
Bz(a,b){var s=a.b
return new A.cm(["Every stair is a different length, and you can't count the steps ahead of time. Have BIT go as far as it can each way until it reaches the portal.","while to the end","Put two whiles inside while not hero.atGoal():. First while hero.canMove('"+s+"'): go "+s+" to the end, then go "+b.b+" to the end.","Endless Stairs"])},
Bx(a,b,c){var s=b===B.bJ?"height of the hill":"depth of the pit",r=a.b
return new A.cm(["Every part of the route is walked the same way; only the "+s+" changes. Write a function with a parameter, and let the caller choose the number.","Functions with parameters","def "+c+"(n): go "+b.b+" n steps, "+r+" one step, back n steps, then "+r+" two steps. Call it three times with different numbers.","Ups and Downs"])},
